<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gian Singh Rarewala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gian Singh Rarewala was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> politician and former official of Patiala State who served as chief minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patiala-and-east-punjab-states-union">Patiala and East Punjab States Union</a> in 1951–1952 and again in 1954–1955. His Akali-supported coalition government of 1952 collapsed, leading to President's rule in 1953.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gian-singh-rarewala.jpg" alt="Gian Singh Rarewala" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gian_Singh_Rarewala_ex_CM.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
